WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.250 --> 00:00:06.259
The economy is collapsing and corona virus
is exploding, and the next three months could

00:00:06.259 --> 00:00:08.360
be a disaster.

00:00:08.360 --> 00:00:12.889
We have now seen the Dow Jones Industrial
Average dropped more than eight percent in

00:00:12.889 --> 00:00:14.400
the last couple of weeks.

00:00:14.400 --> 00:00:20.770
We have seen even after the supposed record
setting, delightful, fantastic GDP numbers

00:00:20.770 --> 00:00:26.289
of the third quarter, we still are down more
than eight points annualized from where we

00:00:26.289 --> 00:00:29.660
were GDP wise before the pandemic.

00:00:29.660 --> 00:00:35.100
We are only getting into what is predicted
to be the worst period in the United States

00:00:35.100 --> 00:00:38.790
from a public health standpoint in literally
100 hundred years.

00:00:38.790 --> 00:00:43.129
Dr. Anthony Foushee said six months ago, if
we don't get this under control.

00:00:43.129 --> 00:00:47.130
We are talking about 100000 cases per day
come fall.

00:00:47.130 --> 00:00:48.899
And Trump has said no way.

00:00:48.899 --> 00:00:50.710
And Republicans said no way.

00:00:50.710 --> 00:00:54.010
And Trump said Foushee doesn't always know
what he's talking about.

00:00:54.010 --> 00:01:00.760
And yet, Friday, we saw for the first time
ever, 100000 cases in a single day, more than

00:01:00.760 --> 00:01:02.899
100, 1000, in fact.

00:01:02.899 --> 00:01:06.590
But what's a thousand cases between friends
at this point?

00:01:06.590 --> 00:01:08.490
But but but the deaths aren't going to climb.

00:01:08.490 --> 00:01:13.540
They said, well, it takes three or more weeks
to see the death numbers climb, but they already

00:01:13.540 --> 00:01:14.540
are.

00:01:14.540 --> 00:01:19.200
As we've seen, the seven day moving average
of deaths bottom out around October 17th and

00:01:19.200 --> 00:01:22.990
start to trickle up, up, up and likely to
continue.

00:01:22.990 --> 00:01:25.360
And this is not because we're doing more testing.

00:01:25.360 --> 00:01:26.700
This is what Trump is claiming.

00:01:26.700 --> 00:01:30.400
We're finding more cases because we've upped
testing.

00:01:30.400 --> 00:01:33.710
Testing is up seven percent in the last week.

00:01:33.710 --> 00:01:36.009
Cases are up 19 percent.

00:01:36.009 --> 00:01:37.369
Testing is up seven percent.

00:01:37.369 --> 00:01:38.369
In the last week.

00:01:38.369 --> 00:01:40.310
Hospitalizations are up 13 percent.

00:01:40.310 --> 00:01:43.590
It is not testing in the month of October.

00:01:43.590 --> 00:01:48.049
Only Georgia and Hawaii saw decreases in hospitalization.

00:01:48.049 --> 00:01:49.790
California was steady.

00:01:49.790 --> 00:01:54.079
Every other state saw increases in hospitalization.

00:01:54.079 --> 00:01:59.649
We have an administration that has no plan
to deal with the virus, but also doesn't even

00:01:59.649 --> 00:02:05.180
understand that if their focus is the economy,
you have to deal with the virus.

00:02:05.180 --> 00:02:10.649
If deaths double to where we're seeing two
thousand twenty five hundred deaths per day

00:02:10.649 --> 00:02:15.010
for one month, two months, three months, things
are going to have to shut down.

00:02:15.010 --> 00:02:17.319
Businesses are going to have to shutter.

00:02:17.319 --> 00:02:19.700
That will be a disaster for the economy.

00:02:19.700 --> 00:02:23.569
Now, Trump may be a lame duck president by
then.

00:02:23.569 --> 00:02:29.650
If he loses tomorrow or he may be reelected
president and rewarded with four more years

00:02:29.650 --> 00:02:31.340
despite having no plan.

00:02:31.340 --> 00:02:37.400
And listen, if he can get reelected with no
plan, you can bet your ass that he's not going

00:02:37.400 --> 00:02:39.430
to then come up with a plan.

00:02:39.430 --> 00:02:40.629
He'll have been reelected.

00:02:40.629 --> 00:02:46.370
He will see it as a referendum that went his
way on his handling of Corona virus.

00:02:46.370 --> 00:02:49.290
So the economy rides on tomorrow's election.

00:02:49.290 --> 00:02:55.130
The handling of the virus and America's public
health rides on the handling of the election.

00:02:55.130 --> 00:02:59.080
Trade policy, international alliances.

00:02:59.080 --> 00:03:03.349
The perception of the United States as a sane
and sensible country.

00:03:03.349 --> 00:03:05.770
It's all riding on tomorrow's election.

00:03:05.770 --> 00:03:12.770
I'll be streaming results live starting at
7:00 p.m. Eastern tomorrow, Tuesday on YouTube,

00:03:12.770 --> 00:03:14.440
Twitch and Facebook.

00:03:14.440 --> 00:03:16.209
I hope you will join me.

00:03:16.209 --> 00:03:20.849
Let me know how your vote went on Twitter,
where you can find me at David Pakman.

